<statement>
<p>
	In conclusion, we say that has a kaprekar number of .
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>Numbers such as 2222 will yield a difference of zero and will never result in 6174. In this case, we say the number of Kaprekar steps is infinity since we will never get there. As such, your program should output</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>inf</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>, MATLAB's notation for infinity.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>For numbers less than 1000, the descending digits must have trailing zeros. For example, if n = 7 (i.e. 0007), then the subtraction step is 7</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>000</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>− 7 = 6993.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>This program should use multiple programs from the previous homework assignment. Make sure you paste a working copy of each of the programs that you want to call at the bottom of this program.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
